an (Traditional), Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"American (New), Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Coffee & Tea, Food","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"nTBStZYJfHGdSZJbpaBiPA","review_id":"KK1MV16ddCm7Po3OK2nLkg","date":"2016-05-30T21:08:49","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9468555450439453,"text_excerpt":"We love this place. We went here on a previous trip, just stumbled upon it, and on this trip we made a point to go back... twice. There are several reasons we love this place, 1. cheap, 2. fast, 3. good, 4. entertaining. The grill is a 50s style diner with a double U serving counter. You are seated when a seat is open at the counter. All of the servers are wearing 50s style uniforms and when you are seated, they give you cloth napkins. Kind of a cool touch. The first day we went, we were there on the early side (around 9am) so we got breakfast. I ordered a Mexican omelette, and my husband got a traditional breakfast (eggs, sausage, toast, hash browns.) Where we were seated, we had an exce..."},{"business_id":"nTBStZYJfHGdSZJbpaBiPA","review_id":"rEVlgjDo9IZVFkXVILdsxg","date":"2011-05-19T20:53:07","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9400172233581543,"text_excerpt":"I loved this place! We came here two times while in NOLA and unlike another (one -time) yelper, I had a great experience as a Latina (and I'm 100% brown, not half white). Let's start from the walk in through the door. It's like a time capsule to the 50's. Everyone is super friendly, singing, cooking, family style seating. It's all so romantically southern, I absolutely loved it. Also the smells of the fresh burger patties and crispy hash browns engulf your system as soon as you walk in. I came in for breakfast (at 2 pm) after a long night of drinking and decided on the Chef's omelet because I had never had an omelet with chili (and I LOVE me some chili). Anyways, the plate is HUGE (eggs +..."},{"business_id":"nTBStZYJfHGdSZJbpaBiPA","review_id":"HUVL0kko4ioQLeDJRVMvpw","date":"2013-02-19T02:11:12","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9360380172729492,"text_excerpt":"I love a good diner, and when this place was recommended to us by our French Quarter tour guide, I was so pumped to try diner food w/ a cajun/creole twist. This place was awesome- I had the turkey omelette done as the mexican omelette (w/ salsa, avocado, etc) and it was fantastic. It came with your basic, delicious hash browns. It was a healthy mix of locals and tourists, the locals all asking about our plans, and telling us how they are always celebrating. One of the servers said, \"Here in New Orleans we celebrate EVERYTHING: getting married, getting divorced, having babies, not having babies, gettin' some on Valentine's Day, not gettin' some on Valentine's Day, getting a job, losing a j..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"nTBStZYJfHGdSZJbpaBiPA","photo_id":"1VBgWpbnP7vWcphaFumHTQ","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/1VBgWpbnP7vWcphaFumHTQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8538259267807007},{"business_id":"nTBStZYJfHGdSZJbpaBiPA","photo_id":